      <h1>Safety and Well-being</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 7 November 2026</p>
      <p>FRIEND CHAT is designed for adults aged 18 and over to meet people through random conversations. A stranger’s identity and intentions may not be known or verified. Please use good judgment and put your safety first.</p>

      <h2>Protect your personal information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Do not share your home address, phone number, passwords, financial details, workplace or real-time location with strangers.</li>
        <li>Be cautious with links, requests for money, investment offers, identity claims and pressure to move to another service.</li>
        <li>Remember that another person may take screenshots or record their own screen, even if the service does not save chat messages in its database.</li>
        <li>Do not send intimate images or anything you would not want copied or shared.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>End an uncomfortable conversation</h2>
      <p>You can leave a conversation at any time. Do not argue with someone who is threatening or harassing you. Keep relevant evidence if it is safe to do so and contact the operators at <a href="mailto:support@friendchat.space">support@friendchat.space</a> with the time, username or other useful details. Do not send intimate images or illegal content as evidence.</p>
      <p>If you believe someone is in immediate danger, contact your local emergency services. FRIEND CHAT is not an emergency-response service.</p>

      <h2>Adults only</h2>
      <p>The service is intended only for people aged 18 or older. Do not use it if you are under 18, and do not encourage a minor to use it or share sexual content involving a minor. The service relies on information users provide and does not currently verify age or identity with official documents.</p>

      <h2>Video and physical well-being</h2>
      <p>The current video-chat page is not yet a working feature. If video chat becomes available, check your camera and microphone settings, avoid showing identifying details in the background, and stop the call whenever you feel uncomfortable. Take breaks and stop using the service if it causes distress, eye strain or fatigue.</p>

      <h2>What the service can and cannot do</h2>
      <p>The service uses basic checks and accepts safety reports, but it does not guarantee that every user or message is screened or that every report is reviewed immediately. Do not rely on the service as a substitute for your own judgment, professional support or emergency help. For privacy information, see our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
